  "note": "Triennial urban council election of May 1961. No newspaper report has been found; the Belfast and Ulster Directory 1962 lists the nine members of the council. Nine members printed (chairman William M. Dunn; vice-chairman Ed. M'Cavana, J.P.). \"J. Mullan\" is printed clearly (re-read on a contrast crop); the 1964 report names a \"former member, J. I. McMullan\", so this is probably J. I. McMullan with the \"Mc\" dropped: check before person matching. Directory list, not an election report: the directory prints the council's membership as it stood when the edition was compiled (late in the year after the election). It does not say whether members were returned at a poll or unopposed, and cannot show co-options made between the election and compilation. No votes."
